From: pokeplatinum-3ds <noreply@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 01:20:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Route 207's edges carried on from its own pieces (SDK_PORT_3DS)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Route 207's east map drawn on past its border in some columns, north and
south (sPortExtrudeColumns, both ways now): its east cliffs over the
mountain's filler north, its cliffs and plateau south, where a black
corner showed. Its west map's rim, which bent west at the map's edge and
ended there, goes on west: the filler's last row left out (sPortMapCuts,
new: a copy of the map drawn in its place while the pieces' map is
loaded) and the map's own rim and ground drawn there (sPortMapPieces,
which repeat east too now: stepX). The east map's lowest ground, which
ended past the map's south edge with no rim, goes on to Oreburgh's rim
height with the map's own rim and corner a tile lower, turning south by
the cliffs.
---
diff --git a/src/overlay005/land_data.c b/src/overlay005/land_data.c
index ee85481c..442f1d40 100644
--- a/src/overlay005/land_data.c
+++ b/src/overlay005/land_data.c
